Verdict: SUPPORTED
Rationale: The claim states that the sub-units using two types of RNA are major components of the unit consisting of ribosomal protein. Evidence supports that ribosomes are composed of approximately 60% ribosomal RNA (rRNA) and 40% ribosomal proteins. Additionally, the two types of RNA used by the sub-units are identified as rRNA and transfer RNA (tRNA). These findings collectively establish the claim without contradiction.
Rounds: 2, findings: 4
Sources:
- Ribosomal RNA, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribosomal_RNA
